Subject: Competitive play: a set called off during its search leaves it
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

A set's game goes into the RANKED search by itself (0056), where the
connection check accepts only the set's opponent. When the set is called off
while the game still searches (the opponent cancelled, or the set ended on
the server), the check had nothing to go by and the search went on as
retail's, so a stranger could be met. SHOnlineMatchmakingDraft::Update now
asks the module (src/platform/competitive_match.cpp) once the search can be
cancelled, and leaves it as the player's Back does (back to the RANKED menu,
then the cancel); until then the module's connection check turns everybody
away.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_competitive.h b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
--- a/include/mscharged_competitive.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
@@ -71,6 +71,12 @@
 bool mscharged_competitive_hides_scene(unsigned long scene);
 #endif
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// The RANKED search screen, while its search can be cancelled: true once a
+// set called off during its search should leave it (tweak patch 0058).
+bool mscharged_competitive_leave_search(void);
+#endif
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
diff --git a/src/Game/SH/SHOnlineMatchmakingDraft.cpp b/src/Game/SH/SHOnlineMatchmakingDraft.cpp
--- a/src/Game/SH/SHOnlineMatchmakingDraft.cpp
